[Auction "N"]
1D 2C pass pass X pass pass pass
[BCFlags "1f"]
[VersionToken "1fe6ae02af8b4ec8126ffe83cc1c91102606052efd50c7657d3213754528c415"]
[Category "Competitive Bidding"]
[Difficulty "intermediate"]
[SkillPath "competitive_bidding/negative_doubles"]
[Student "S"]
{The bidding has been as shown.   

First let's agree on what you <b>DON'T</b> say. You don't say "double" because that would a Negative Double showing at least one 4-card Major. You don't support partner's \Ds with just two of them. You probably don't bid 1NT with no honor in either Major. So you pass. This is called a "Trap Pass". Partner re-opens with a double.  

Now you see why it's called a "Trap Pass". When an overcall is followed by two passes Opener should try to find another bid. In particular he should try to double for takeout if he can. That's what North did here, but you converted it to a Penalty Double by passing.}
[Play "S"]
DA

